<p><a href="https://grahampriest.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Graham Priest</a>, currently Distinguished Professor of Philosophy at <a href="https://www.gc.cuny.edu/philosophy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">City University of New York</a> (CUNY) Graduate Center, will be moving to <a href="https://www.tohoku.ac.jp/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tohoku University</a> in Japan.<span id="more-57683"></span></p>
<p><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="wp-image-57684 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/priest-graham.png" alt="" width="600" height="600" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/priest-graham.png 1080w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/priest-graham-300x300.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/priest-graham-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/priest-graham-150x150.png 150w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/priest-graham-768x768.png 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/priest-graham-400x400.png 400w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/priest-graham-177x177.png 177w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/priest-graham-380x380.png 380w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" /></p>
<p>Professor Priest is known for his work in logic, especially non-classical logic, as well as philosophy of math, metaphysics, Buddhist philosophy, and the history of philosophy. You can learn more about his writings <a href="https://grahampriest.net/publications/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a> and <a href="https://philpeople.org/profiles/graham-priest" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p>
<p>He will be taking up his new position as Distinguished Professor in the <a href="https://www.is.tohoku.ac.jp/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Graduate School of Information Sciences</a> at Tohoku University in October.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/06/25/priest-from-cuny-to-tohoku/">Priest from CUNY to Tohoku</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>